    {
      "id": "claim_beada14d1b814c97b08828ebda581653",
      "statement": "The bootstrap is bash .openinspect/setup.sh: it checks Node.js ≥ 20 and npm, runs npm install (husky hooks via prepare), builds @open-inspect/shared first, verifies git hooks, and — when Python ≥ 3.12 and uv are available — syncs the modal-infra Python environment via uv sync --frozen --extra dev (falling back to pip editable installs of packages/sandbox-runtime and packages/modal-infra[dev]), finishing with npm run typecheck.",
